Starting nc:
`docker exec -d dev_nginx sh -c 'exec nc -lk -p 18999 -e /tmp/agent-hub-sse-verify/serve.sh'` — with `exec`, the shell is replaced by nc, so `docker exec` process is nc; but `-d` detaches. `docker exec -d` starts and returns. To kill later, we need PID. Options:
